# The server image (Server/Dockerfile) only ever COPYs Assets/Scripts/Sim,
# Assets/Scripts/Net, and Server/Craftwar.NetServer, but `docker build`
# hashes and uploads the WHOLE build context before a single COPY runs — so
# without this file, a `docker build -f Server/Dockerfile .` from the repo
# root would spend minutes on Unity's Library/ cache (routinely multiple
# GB) before the build even starts. Kept simple (exclude the few huge/
# irrelevant top-level dirs) rather than trying to allowlist a narrow
# subtree — Docker's ignore matcher does not reliably support "exclude a
# directory, then re-include one of its descendants".
[Ll]ibrary/
[Tt]emp/
[Oo]bj/
[Bb]uild/
[Bb]uilds/
[Ll]ogs/
[Uu]ser[Ss]ettings/
[Mm]emoryCaptures/
[Rr]ecordings/
.vs/
.idea/
.git/

# Blizzard-owned data must never leave this machine, let alone into a
# Docker image layer — see CLAUDE.md's licensing guardrails. Not needed for
# the server build anyway (it only touches Sim/Net source).
/Assets/GameData/Extracted/
/Assets/StreamingAssets/Maps/*.pud

Server/**/bin/
Server/**/obj/
Server/**/*.db
Server/**/*.db-shm
Server/**/*.db-wal
Server/**/*.pfx
